From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Caleb E." <158400752+FoxesRCool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:06:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus: power the DMICs from vdd-micb

The Surface Laptop 7's digital microphones record nothing usable: one
channel is full-scale noise and the other carries no sound. The VA
macro powers DMICs from its vdd-micb supply (vreg_l1b), but the sound
card routes VA DMIC0 and DMIC1 to the WCD938x's MIC BIAS3 and to
"VA MIC BIAS3", which the VA macro doesn't have. Nothing asks for
vdd-micb, so vreg_l1b stays off while recording and the microphones
run unpowered.

Route both DMICs to vdd-micb and clock them at 2.4 MHz, as the Surface
Pro 11's tree (x1-microsoft-denali.dtsi) does for the same VA macro,
pins and supply.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 13.8" (X1E80100) from a hw-test boot
entry on linux-omarchy 7.3.0-75: vdd-micb turns on with a capture,
DMIC0 and DMIC1 both carry room sound (correlated between channels),
and a 1 kHz tone from the speakers rises from about 16 to about 1200 in
both channels of PipeWire's "Internal microphones" source, through
alsa-ucm-conf's Surface Laptop 7 profile. DMIC2 and DMIC3 stay silent
with their pins muxed and powered, so the 13.8" has its two microphones
on DMIC0 and DMIC1. The 15" shares this dtsi and hasn't been tested.
The 2.4 MHz clock wasn't tested apart from the supply change.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
index 2537a10..6679e1f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus.dtsi
@@ -375,10 +375,8 @@
 				"IN1_HPHL", "HPHL_OUT",
 				"IN2_HPHR", "HPHR_OUT",
 				"AMIC2", "MIC BIAS2",
-				"VA DMIC0", "MIC BIAS3",
-				"VA DMIC1", "MIC BIAS3",
-				"VA DMIC0", "VA MIC BIAS3",
-				"VA DMIC1", "VA MIC BIAS3",
+				"VA DMIC0", "vdd-micb",
+				"VA DMIC1", "vdd-micb",
 				"TX SWR_INPUT1", "ADC2_OUTPUT";
 
 		displayport-0-dai-link {
@@ -1058,7 +1056,7 @@
 };
 
 &lpass_vamacro {
-	qcom,dmic-sample-rate = <4800000>;
+	qcom,dmic-sample-rate = <2400000>;
 
 	vdd-micb-supply = <&vreg_l1b>;
 
